# The license inventory and the file rendered from it must be byte-identical on
# every platform: `npm run notices:check` compares a fresh render against the
# committed copy, and a CRLF checkout makes that comparison fail on Windows and
# nowhere else. It did — one upstream text (libopenmpt's) ships with CRLF, git
# normalised it in the blob while leaving the working copy alone, and the Windows
# runner then checked every one of these files out as CRLF.
#
# `gen-notices.mjs` also normalises on read, so the gate no longer depends on
# this file. Both are kept: the script guarantees the comparison, this guarantees
# the working copies match their blobs, and neither is a substitute for the other.
LICENSE                 text eol=lf
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md  text eol=lf
licenses/**             text eol=lf
